{
  "_comment": [
    "Fixture Blueprint for the row-scoping tests. ONE source for both halves:",
    "run-ownership-tests.sh renders src/lib/ownership-rules.ts from this doc with",
    "the real projection, and ownership-scope.test.mts builds its tables and rows",
    "from the same entities. A test that hand-wrote the manifest would pass while",
    "the projection emitted something else.",
    "",
    "Invoice is scoped to its owner, with admin exempt. Announcement carries an",
    "attribution rule: postedByUserId is filled from the session but must never",
    "narrow a read - the case a name-based heuristic would get wrong, and the one",
    "the live ATS blueprint depends on. Ticket is drift: the rule names a column",
    "the table does not carry, and the engine has to fail closed on it.",
    "",
    "RefundCase is scoped to a workspace: propertyId is compared to the users",
    "column the rule names (actorColumn: homePropertyId), so a hotel group whose",
    "managers sit at a home property reads only that property's cases. Finance",
    "is exempt. Without actorColumn the engine fell back to a workspaceId the",
    "session did not carry and every property-scoped read returned nothing.",
    "",
    "Child is scoped to its parent (parentId); Appointment carries no owner column",
    "and is reached THROUGH its child: childId must be one of the actor's children.",
    "Kids Vaccination Tracker's parents saw no appointments when the rule named a",
    "parentId the appointments table never had (forge-v3, 2026-09-26)."
  ],
